;;; A goal's guard written before the premise that binds its variable is
;;; judged on a null — M1f **W55**, register row
;;; `W55/goal-guard-before-binder` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`), filed by
;;; S1f.5.7 (T1f.5.7.1, 2026-11-09) from its step 1, `open` and owned by
;;; S1f.5.7, on the user's ruling of 2026-11-07 (Q-M1e2.26: a conjunction means
;;; the same in any order of its conjuncts).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; One fact `(p a)` and a query whose goal is `(and (neq a ?y) (p ?y))`, with
;;; the claim that its one class is empty.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The goal is `(and (p ?y) (neq a ?y))`: `(p ?y)` binds `?y` to `a`, and
;;; `(neq a a)` is false, so the goal has no row, its class is `(model)`, and
;;; the claim holds: exit 0.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The guard is judged where it is written, comparing `a` with an unbound
;;; `?y` as with a null, which differs, so it holds, and `(p ?y)` then binds
;;; `?y` to `a`: one row, `?y = a`, the class `(model (neq a a) (p a))`, and
;;; the claim is FAILED, exit 1 (`ein solve FILE` at `dc4c0bdc`, release and
;;; debug alike).

(relation p Node :why "{?1} is a node")
(p a)
(query :goal (and (neq a ?y) (p ?y))
  :expect (model))
